      see_also    : "https://workbench.cisecurity.org/benchmarks/22176"
      value_type  : POLICY_DWORD
      value_data  : "3"
      reg_key     : "HKLM\Software\Policies\Microsoft\Windows NT\Terminal Services"
      reg_item    : "MinEncryptionLevel"
      reg_option  : CAN_NOT_BE_NULL
    </custom_item>

    <custom_item>
      type        : REGISTRY_SETTING
      description : "1.132 WN19-CC-000390"
      info        : "Windows Server 2019 must prevent attachments from being downloaded from RSS feeds.

GROUP ID:V-205873
RULE ID:SV-205873r991589

Attachments from RSS feeds may not be secure. This setting will prevent attachments from being downloaded from RSS feeds."
      solution    : 'Configure the policy value for

Computer Configuration >> Administrative Templates >> Windows Components >> RSS Feeds >> \'Prevent downloading of enclosures\' to \'Enabled\'.'
      reference   : "800-171|3.4.2,800-171r3|03.04.02a.,800-53|CM-6b.,800-53r5|CM-6b.,CAT|II,CCI|CCI-000366,CN-L3|8.1.10.6(d),CSF|PR.IP-1,CSF2.0|DE.CM-09,CSF2.0|PR.PS-01,GDPR|32.1.b,HIPAA|164.306(a)(1),ISO-27001-2022|A.8.9,ITSG-33|CM-6b.,LEVEL|2A,NESA|T3.2.1,Rule-ID|SV-205873r991589_rule,STIG-ID|WN19-CC-000390,SWIFT-CSCv1|2.3"
      see_also    : "https://workbench.cisecurity.org/benchmarks/22176"
      value_type  : POLICY_DWORD
      value_data  : "1"
      reg_key     : "HKLM\Software\Policies\Microsoft\Internet Explorer\Feeds"
      reg_item    : "DisableEnclosureDownload"
      reg_option  : CAN_NOT_BE_NULL
    </custom_item>

    <custom_item>
      type        : REGISTRY_SETTING
      description : "1.133 WN19-CC-000400"
      info        : "Windows Server 2019 must disable Basic authentication for RSS feeds over HTTP.

GROUP ID:V-205693
RULE ID:SV-205693r958478

Basic authentication uses plain-text passwords that could be used to compromise a system. Disabling Basic authentication will reduce this potential."
      solution    : 'The default behavior is for the Windows RSS platform to not use Basic authentication over HTTP connections.

If this needs to be corrected, configure the policy value for

Computer Configuration >> Administrative Templates >> Windows Components >> RSS Feeds >> \'Turn on Basic feed authentication over HTTP\' to \'Not Configured\' or \'Disabled\'.'
      reference   : "800-171|3.4.6,800-171|3.4.7,800-171r3|03.04.06,800-171r3|03.04.06a.,800-53|CM-7,800-53|CM-7a.,800-53r5|CM-7a.,CAT|II,CCI|CCI-000381,CN-L3|7.1.3.5(c),CN-L3|8.1.4.4(a),CSF|PR.IP-1,CSF|PR.PT-3,CSF2.0|PR.PS-01,GDPR|32.1.b,HIPAA|164.306(a)(1),ITSG-33|CM-7,ITSG-33|CM-7a.,LEVEL|2A,NIAv2|SS15a,PCI-DSSv3.2.1|2.2.1,PCI-DSSv3.2.1|2.2.2,PCI-DSSv4.0|2.2.3,QCSC-v1|3.2,Rule-ID|SV-205693r958478_rule,STIG-ID|WN19-CC-000400,SWIFT-CSCv1|2.3"
      see_also    : "https://workbench.cisecurity.org/benchmarks/22176"
      value_type  : POLICY_DWORD
      value_data  : "0"
      reg_key     : "HKLM\Software\Policies\Microsoft\Internet Explorer\Feeds"
      reg_item    : "AllowBasicAuthInClear"
      reg_option  : CAN_BE_NULL
    </custom_item>

    <custom_item>
      type        : REGISTRY_SETTING
      description : "1.134 WN19-CC-000410"
      info        : "Windows Server 2019 must prevent Indexing of encrypted files.

GROUP ID:V-205694
RULE ID:SV-205694r958478

Indexing of encrypted files may expose sensitive data. This setting prevents encrypted files from being indexed."
      solution    : 'Configure the policy value for

Computer Configuration >> Administrative Templates >> Windows Components >> Search >> \'Allow indexing of encrypted files\' to \'Disabled\'.'
      reference   : "800-171|3.4.6,800-171|3.4.7,800-171r3|03.04.06,800-171r3|03.04.06a.,800-53|CM-7,800-53|CM-7a.,800-53r5|CM-7a.,CAT|II,CCI|CCI-000381,CN-L3|7.1.3.5(c),CN-L3|8.1.4.4(a),CSF|PR.IP-1,CSF|PR.PT-3,CSF2.0|PR.PS-01,GDPR|32.1.b,HIPAA|164.306(a)(1),ITSG-33|CM-7,ITSG-33|CM-7a.,LEVEL|2A,NIAv2|SS15a,PCI-DSSv3.2.1|2.2.1,PCI-DSSv3.2.1|2.2.2,PCI-DSSv4.0|2.2.3,QCSC-v1|3.2,Rule-ID|SV-205694r958478_rule,STIG-ID|WN19-CC-000410,SWIFT-CSCv1|2.3"
      see_also    : "https://workbench.cisecurity.org/benchmarks/22176"
      value_type  : POLICY_DWORD
