Computer Configuration >> Administrative Templates >> Windows Components >> Windows Installer >> \'Allow user control over installs\' to \'Disabled\'.'
      reference   : "800-171|3.4.9,800-53|CM-11(2),800-53r5|CM-11(2),CAT|II,CCI|CCI-001812,CCI|CCI-003980,CSF|DE.CM-3,CSF2.0|DE.CM-03,CSF2.0|DE.CM-09,CSF2.0|PR.PS-01,CSF2.0|PR.PS-02,GDPR|32.1.b,HIPAA|164.306(a)(1),ISO-27001-2022|A.8.19,ISO/IEC-27001|A.12.6.2,LEVEL|2A,QCSC-v1|8.2.1,Rule-ID|SV-205801r1051078_rule,STIG-ID|WN19-CC-000420,SWIFT-CSCv1|5.1"
