      <then>
        <custom_item>
          type            : AUDIT_POWERSHELL
          description     : "1.159 WN19-DC-000130"
          info            : "Windows Server 2019 domain controllers must run on a machine dedicated to that function.

GROUP ID:V-205695
RULE ID:SV-205695r958478

Executing application servers on the same host machine with a directory server may substantially weaken the security of the directory server. Web or database server applications usually require the addition of many programs and accounts, increasing the attack surface of the computer.

Some applications require the addition of privileged accounts, providing potential sources of compromise. Some applications (such as Microsoft Exchange) may require the use of network ports or services conflicting with the directory server. In this case, non-standard ports might be selected, and this could interfere with intrusion detection or prevention services.

NOTE: Nessus has provided the target output to assist in reviewing the benchmark to ensure target compliance."
          solution        : "Remove additional roles or applications such as web, database, and email from the domain controller."
          reference       : "800-171|3.4.6,800-171|3.4.7,800-171r3|03.04.06,800-171r3|03.04.06a.,800-53|CM-7,800-53|CM-7a.,800-53r5|CM-7a.,CAT|II,CCI|CCI-000381,CN-L3|7.1.3.5(c),CN-L3|8.1.4.4(a),CSF|PR.IP-1,CSF|PR.PT-3,CSF2.0|PR.PS-01,GDPR|32.1.b,HIPAA|164.306(a)(1),ITSG-33|CM-7,ITSG-33|CM-7a.,LEVEL|2M,NIAv2|SS15a,PCI-DSSv3.2.1|2.2.1,PCI-DSSv3.2.1|2.2.2,PCI-DSSv4.0|2.2.3,QCSC-v1|3.2,Rule-ID|SV-205695r958478_rule,STIG-ID|WN19-DC-000130,SWIFT-CSCv1|2.3"
          see_also        : "https://workbench.cisecurity.org/benchmarks/22176"
          value_type      : POLICY_TEXT
          value_data      : "^Manual Review Required$"
          powershell_args : "Get-WindowsFeature | Where {$_.InstallState -eq 'Installed'} | Where {$_.Name -ne 'AD-Domain-Services'} | Where {$_.Name -ne 'DNS'}  | Where {$_.Name -ne 'FileAndStorage-Services'}"
          check_type      : CHECK_REGEX
          severity        : MEDIUM
        </custom_item>
      </then>

      <else>
        <report type:"PASSED">
          description : "1.159 WN19-DC-000130"
          info        : "Windows Server 2019 domain controllers must run on a machine dedicated to that function.

GROUP ID:V-205695
RULE ID:SV-205695r958478

Executing application servers on the same host machine with a directory server may substantially weaken the security of the directory server. Web or database server applications usually require the addition of many programs and accounts, increasing the attack surface of the computer.

Some applications require the addition of privileged accounts, providing potential sources of compromise. Some applications (such as Microsoft Exchange) may require the use of network ports or services conflicting with the directory server. In this case, non-standard ports might be selected, and this could interfere with intrusion detection or prevention services."
          solution    : "Remove additional roles or applications such as web, database, and email from the domain controller."
          reference   : "800-171|3.4.6,800-171|3.4.7,800-171r3|03.04.06,800-171r3|03.04.06a.,800-53|CM-7,800-53|CM-7a.,800-53r5|CM-7a.,CAT|II,CCI|CCI-000381,CN-L3|7.1.3.5(c),CN-L3|8.1.4.4(a),CSF|PR.IP-1,CSF|PR.PT-3,CSF2.0|PR.PS-01,GDPR|32.1.b,HIPAA|164.306(a)(1),ITSG-33|CM-7,ITSG-33|CM-7a.,LEVEL|2M,NIAv2|SS15a,PCI-DSSv3.2.1|2.2.1,PCI-DSSv3.2.1|2.2.2,PCI-DSSv4.0|2.2.3,QCSC-v1|3.2,Rule-ID|SV-205695r958478_rule,STIG-ID|WN19-DC-000130,SWIFT-CSCv1|2.3"
          see_also    : "https://workbench.cisecurity.org/benchmarks/22176"
        </report>
      </else>
    </if>

    <custom_item>
      type            : AUDIT_POWERSHELL
      description     : "1.16 WN19-00-000160"
      info            : 'Windows Server 2019 permissions for the Windows installation directory must conform to minimum requirements.

GROUP ID:V-205736
RULE ID:SV-205736r1016383

Changing the system\'s file and directory permissions allows the possibility of unauthorized and anonymous modification to the operating system and installed applications.

The default permissions are adequate when the Security Option \'Network access: Let Everyone permissions apply to anonymous users\' is set to \'Disabled\' (WN19-SO-000240).

Satisfies: SRG-OS-000312-GPOS-00122, SRG-OS-000312-GPOS-00123, SRG-OS-000312-GPOS-00124'
      solution        : 'Maintain the default file ACLs and configure the Security Option \'Network access: Let Everyone permissions apply to anonymous users\' to \'Disabled\' (WN19-SO-000240).

Default permissions:Type - \'Allow\' for allInherited from - \'None\' for all

Principal - Access - Applies to

 - TrustedInstaller - Full control - This folder and subfolders
 - SYSTEM - Modify - This folder only
 - SYSTEM - Full control - Subfolders and files only
 - Administrators - Modify - This folder only
 - Administrators - Full control - Subfolders and files only
 - Users - Read & execute - This folder, subfolders, and files
 - CREATOR OWNER - Full control - Subfolders and files only
 - ALL APPLICATION PACKAGES - Read & execute - This folder, subfolders, and files
 - ALL RESTRICTED APPLICATION PACKAGES - Read & execute - This folder, subfolders, and files'
      reference       : "800-171|3.1.1,800-171r3|03.01.02,800-53|AC-3(4),800-53r5|AC-3(4),CAT|II,CCI|CCI-002165,CN-L3|8.1.4.2(f),CN-L3|8.1.4.11(b),CN-L3|8.1.10.2(c),CN-L3|8.5.3.1,CN-L3|8.5.4.1(a),CSF|PR.AC-4,CSF|PR.PT-3,CSF2.0|PR.AA-05,CSF2.0|PR.DS-10,CSF2.0|PR.IR-01,GDPR|32.1.b,HIPAA|164.306(a)(1),HIPAA|164.312(a)(1),ISO-27001-2022|A.5.15,ISO-27001-2022|A.5.33,ISO-27001-2022|A.8.3,ISO-27001-2022|A.8.18,ISO-27001-2022|A.8.20,ISO/IEC-27001|A.9.4.1,ISO/IEC-27001|A.9.4.5,ITSG-33|AC-3(4),LEVEL|2M,NESA|T4.2.1,NESA|T5.4.4,NESA|T5.4.5,NESA|T5.5.4,NESA|T5.6.1,NESA|T7.5.2,NESA|T7.5.3,NIAv2|AM3,NIAv2|SS29,QCSC-v1|3.2,QCSC-v1|5.2.2,QCSC-v1|13.2,Rule-ID|SV-205736r1016383_rule,STIG-ID|WN19-00-000160,TBA-FIISB|31.1"
      see_also        : "https://workbench.cisecurity.org/benchmarks/22176"
      value_type      : POLICY_TEXT
      value_data      : "STATUS: PASSED"
      powershell_args : "$f = $env:SystemRoot;
      $acls = (icacls $f);
      $status = 'PASSED';
      foreach ($acl in $acls) {
        if (!$acl) { continue }
        elseif ($acl -like '*NT SERVICE\TrustedInstaller:(F)') { continue }
        elseif ($acl -like '*NT SERVICE\TrustedInstaller:(CI)(IO)(F)') { continue }
        elseif ($acl -like '*NT AUTHORITY\SYSTEM:*(M)') { continue }
        elseif ($acl -like '*NT AUTHORITY\SYSTEM:*(OI)(CI)(IO)(F)') { continue }
        elseif ($acl -like '*BUILTIN\Administrators:*(M)') { continue }
        elseif ($acl -like '*BUILTIN\Administrators:*(OI)(CI)(IO)(F)') { continue }
        elseif ($acl -like '*BUILTIN\Users:*(RX)') { continue }
        elseif ($acl -like '*BUILTIN\Users:*(OI)(CI)(IO)(GR,GE)') { continue }
        elseif ($acl -like '*CREATOR OWNER:*(OI)(CI)(IO)(F)') { continue }
        elseif ($acl -like '*APPLICATION PACKAGE AUTHORITY\ALL APPLICATION PACKAGES:*(RX)') { continue }
        elseif ($acl -like '*APPLICATION PACKAGE AUTHORITY\ALL APPLICATION PACKAGES:*(OI)(CI)(IO)(GR,GE)') { continue }
        elseif ($acl -like '*APPLICATION PACKAGE AUTHORITY\ALL RESTRICTED APPLICATION PACKAGES:*(RX)') { continue }
        elseif ($acl -like '*APPLICATION PACKAGE AUTHORITY\ALL RESTRICTED APPLICATION PACKAGES:*(OI)(CI)(IO)(GR,GE)') { continue }
        elseif ($acl -like 'Successfully processed*') { continue }
        $status = 'FAILED'
      }
      $acls;
      '';
      'STATUS: '+$status"
      check_type      : CHECK_REGEX
    </custom_item>

