          type        : REGISTRY_SETTING
          description : "1.178 WN19-DC-000330"
          info        : "Windows Server 2019 domain controllers must be configured to allow reset of machine account passwords.

GROUP ID: V-205876
RULE ID: SV-205876r991589

Enabling this setting on all domain controllers in a domain prevents domain members from changing their computer account passwords. If these passwords are weak or compromised, the inability to change them may leave these computers vulnerable."
          solution    : 'Configure the policy value for

Computer Configuration >> Windows Settings >> Security Settings >> Local Policies >> Security Options >> \'Domain controller: Refuse machine account password changes\' to \'Disabled\'.'
          reference   : "800-171|3.4.2,800-171r3|03.04.02a.,800-53|CM-6b.,800-53r5|CM-6b.,CAT|II,CCI|CCI-000366,CN-L3|8.1.10.6(d),CSF|PR.IP-1,CSF2.0|DE.CM-09,CSF2.0|PR.PS-01,GDPR|32.1.b,HIPAA|164.306(a)(1),ISO-27001-2022|A.8.9,ITSG-33|CM-6b.,LEVEL|2A,NESA|T3.2.1,Rule-ID|SV-205876r991589_rule,STIG-ID|WN19-DC-000330,SWIFT-CSCv1|2.3,Vuln-ID|V-205876"
          see_also    : "https://workbench.cisecurity.org/benchmarks/22176"
          value_type  : POLICY_DWORD
          value_data  : "0"
          reg_key     : "HKLM\System\CurrentControlSet\Services\Netlogon\Parameters"
          reg_item    : "RefusePasswordChange"
          reg_option  : CAN_NOT_BE_NULL
        </custom_item>
      </then>

