      <then>
        <custom_item>
          type            : AUDIT_POWERSHELL
          description     : "1.6 WN19-00-000060"
          info            : "Windows Server 2019 manually managed application account passwords must be changed at least annually or when a system administrator with knowledge of the password leaves the organization.

GROUP ID:V-205847
RULE ID:SV-205847r991589

Setting application account passwords to expire may cause applications to stop functioning. However, not changing them on a regular basis exposes them to attack. If managed service accounts are used, this alleviates the need to manually change application account passwords."
          solution        : "Change passwords for manually managed application/service accounts at least annually or when an administrator with knowledge of the password leaves the organization.

It is recommended that system-managed service accounts be used whenever possible."
          reference       : "800-171|3.4.2,800-171r3|03.04.02a.,800-53|CM-6b.,800-53r5|CM-6b.,CAT|II,CCI|CCI-000366,CN-L3|8.1.10.6(d),CSF|PR.IP-1,CSF2.0|DE.CM-09,CSF2.0|PR.PS-01,GDPR|32.1.b,HIPAA|164.306(a)(1),ISO-27001-2022|A.8.9,ITSG-33|CM-6b.,LEVEL|2M,NESA|T3.2.1,Rule-ID|SV-205847r991589_rule,STIG-ID|WN19-00-000060,SWIFT-CSCv1|2.3"
          see_also        : "https://workbench.cisecurity.org/benchmarks/22176"
          value_type      : POLICY_TEXT
          value_data      : "No service account with password older than 365 days"
          powershell_args : "$svc_accts = @('@MAN_SVC_ACCT@'); $flagged = @(); foreach ($id in $svc_accts) { $flagged += Get-ADUser -Filter {SamAccountName -eq $id } -Properties PasswordLastSet | Where {$_.PasswordLastSet -le (Get-Date).AddDays(-@PASSWORD_LAST_SET@)} | Format-Table -Property name, SID, PasswordLastSet }; if ($flagged) { $flagged } else { 'No service account with password older than @PASSWORD_LAST_SET@ days' };"
          check_type      : CHECK_REGEX
        </custom_item>
      </then>

      <else>
        <custom_item>
          type            : AUDIT_POWERSHELL
          description     : "1.6 WN19-00-000060"
          info            : "Windows Server 2019 manually managed application account passwords must be changed at least annually or when a system administrator with knowledge of the password leaves the organization.

GROUP ID:V-205847
RULE ID:SV-205847r991589

Setting application account passwords to expire may cause applications to stop functioning. However, not changing them on a regular basis exposes them to attack. If managed service accounts are used, this alleviates the need to manually change application account passwords."
          solution        : "Change passwords for manually managed application/service accounts at least annually or when an administrator with knowledge of the password leaves the organization.

It is recommended that system-managed service accounts be used whenever possible."
          reference       : "800-171|3.4.2,800-171r3|03.04.02a.,800-53|CM-6b.,800-53r5|CM-6b.,CAT|II,CCI|CCI-000366,CN-L3|8.1.10.6(d),CSF|PR.IP-1,CSF2.0|DE.CM-09,CSF2.0|PR.PS-01,GDPR|32.1.b,HIPAA|164.306(a)(1),ISO-27001-2022|A.8.9,ITSG-33|CM-6b.,LEVEL|2M,NESA|T3.2.1,Rule-ID|SV-205847r991589_rule,STIG-ID|WN19-00-000060,SWIFT-CSCv1|2.3"
          see_also        : "https://workbench.cisecurity.org/benchmarks/22176"
          value_type      : POLICY_TEXT
          value_data      : "No service account with password older than 365 days"
          powershell_args : "$svc_accts = @('@MAN_SVC_ACCT@'); $adsi = [ADSI]'WinNT://localhost'; $users = $adsi.Children | Where-Object { $svc_accts -contains $_.Name } | where {$_.PassWordAge -gt 86400*@PASSWORD_LAST_SET@} | ForEach { [pscustomobject]@{ Username = $_.Name; PasswordAgeInDays = [math]::Round($_.PasswordAge/86400) } }; if ($users) { ForEach ($user in $users) { $user | Format-Table } } Else { 'No service account with password older than @PASSWORD_LAST_SET@ days' }"
        </custom_item>
      </else>
    </if>

